      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WILUNA LASS (3) is the runner to beat after winning both starts this campaign, first beating STAR MARTINI in a CL1 at Belmont and then holding on by a nose as favourite in a CL2 at Kalgoorlie. Coming back to 1000m looks a smart move and she can find the front from a good draw. Will be hard to catch with Taylor's claim helping. STAR MARTINI (4) is the clear danger, having finished second at her past two and already won at this track and distance. She was beaten just over a length by WILUNA LASS last time and now meets her worse at the weights, but Nottle replaces the apprentice hoop and she can stalk WILUNA LASS' every move. NATURE'S RECKONING (1) resumes after five months and brings stronger form from last campaign. No trial coming in but she can be thereabouts. MANTUA (5) backs up quickly after a close third at York, gets weight relief and is honest enough to press for a minor money finish if he repeats that effort. SO IMMACULATE (6) won't be far away coming back in trip.",
